@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) is that standard, and later features (e.g. JSON Patch, RFC 6902) build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the value a JSON Pointer string refers to.
+- It throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3) or does not resolve to a value in the document (§4).
+- Add the project's first source files (`src/`) and tests runnable with `npm test`.
+- Not breaking: this is a new export; nothing existing changes.
+
+**Governing standard:** RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer), §3 syntax, §4 evaluation, §5 JSON string representation. The URI fragment representation (§6) is out of scope.
+
+**Out of scope:** URI fragment form (`#/a`), setting/removing values, JSON Patch, relative pointers, pointer construction/escaping helpers.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: parsing and evaluating RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New: `src/index.ts` (and an implementation module), tests under `src/`. No dependencies added, `package.json` unchanged.
